1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:01,850
Oleg, hi.

2
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:12,530
I wanted to show you another clip about how the pulse moves, how it works on the magnetic field.

3
00:00:13,270 --> 00:00:20,950
We see the current component as a sine wave, slightly curved.

4
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:22,730
And the pulses.

5
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:24,270
What am I doing?

6
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:28,150
The pulses are measured directly from the transistor's gate.

7
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:31,990
And I'll apply voltage to the transistor right now.

8
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:33,090
Watch what happens.

9
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:33,930
See?

10
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:39,550
The sine wave shifts in antiphase.

11
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:48,930
If I now move these pulses to a different place, I'll flip them around.

12
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:49,350
Here, look.

13
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,290
Now I'll flip them around.

14
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,050
I'll put them like this.

15
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:59,410
Now they come out in phase.

16
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:03,910
And here's what we get when we connect the voltage.

17
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:05,250
See?

18
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:10,930
Something's happening, but the field stays in place.

19
00:01:11,990 --> 00:01:13,790
It doesn't move either way.

20
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:17,930
This way we don't get anything.

21
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:26,930
All this tells us we need to give these pulses in antiphase.

22
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:29,270
We put the jumper the other way.

23
00:01:31,030 --> 00:01:35,810
And, as it was for me before, we make antiphase.

24
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:37,550
It shifts over here.

25
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:41,510
This way, by connecting…

26
00:01:41,510 --> 00:01:43,430
Watch what happens.

27
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:44,570
See?

28
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:46,550
Immediately some kind of movement happens.

29
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:49,570
It's not strong, that's why the power is small.

30
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:53,030
This beard here, see?

31
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:54,270
It shifts.

32
00:01:55,230 --> 00:01:57,870
Everything moves, absolutely, everything slides around on the oscilloscope.

33
00:02:00,050 --> 00:02:03,670
There's movement, and the frequency changes.

34
00:02:03,910 --> 00:02:06,030
I mean the frequency drifts by 20 kHz.

35
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:07,990
Right off to the side.

36
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:10,710
See what's happening?

37
00:02:12,810 --> 00:02:20,670
This tells us that there's movement of the magnetic field under the influence of a high-voltage pulse.

38
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:26,630
By the way, you can apply even the weakest pulse and there's still movement, and very strong at that.

39
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:29,350
I mean the frequency darts back and forth.

40
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:33,430
Well, something like that for now.

41
00:02:33,650 --> 00:02:36,810
But I'm working, working, working, working.

42
00:02:37,570 --> 00:02:39,490
Soon I'll show what I've come up with.
